+## Build on Windows 11 x64
+
+Required: Visual Studio 2022 C++ desktop workload and Windows SDK, CMake, Git/Git
+Bash, Python 3.11 with `autobuild` and `llsd`, and access to the upstream binary
+dependency download servers. The bundled autobuild.xml owns library versions.
+Install Python tooling with `python -m pip install autobuild llsd`.
+
+Open an x64 VS developer environment, launch Git Bash inheriting it, and run:
+
+```bash
+bash kombatant/build-windows.sh
+```
+
+The script selects ReleaseOS, OpenAL audio, no KDU, no proprietary build mode,
+no upstream crash-report database, and no installer packaging. This script has
+been shell-syntax checked only. The upstream dependencies and actual Windows
+compile/link still need verification. Media, voice and audio also need runtime
+checks. The existing GitHub build workflow is upstream's workflow and is not a
+validated Kombatant release pipeline.
