+## 12K photo output (0.2)
+
+The Save to Disk snapshot dropdown now offers 12,288 x 6,912 (16:9),
+84,934,656 pixels. Upstream's 11,520 x 6,480 option labeled 12K is replaced.
+The snapshot dimension cap and unlocked width/height controls are aligned at
+12,288. Studio has a snapshot button and brief instructions.
+
+After building: open Studio > Open snapshots / 12K photos, select Save to Disk,
+enable Allow High Resolutions, disable inclusion of UI and HUD, then choose
+12288x6912 (12K). Select PNG and refresh the snapshot before saving. For this
+16:9 preset, disable Constrain proportions if the window has a different aspect
+ratio. The renderer's existing allocation checks and tiled fallback remain.
+
+12K is saved-image resolution; gameplay rendering stays at window resolution.
+Photo detail remains limited by loaded textures, meshes, lighting and the
+existing renderer. No AI upscaling or texture reconstruction was added. A single
+RGB output buffer is about 243 MiB; render targets, encoding and previews need
+additional memory. Successful capture, exact saved dimensions, seams and visual
+quality still require Windows runtime testing. No 12K runtime image was produced
+in this environment.
+
+## Experimental live 12K rendering (0.3)
+
+Studio now has a Live World Rendering selector: Window / 4K / 8K / 12K.
+This controls main-world offscreen render target width, not snapshot resolution.
+At a 16:9 viewport, 12K requests 12,288 x 6,912 pixels every frame. Other window
+shapes preserve their own aspect ratio. The final world image is sampled to the
+physical window; the monitor does not gain pixels and UI remains window-sized.
+
+The main render allocation and resize comparison share the same size calculation.
+Scaling is applied once, fixing upstream's repeated scaling on resize. Reflection
+probe buffers retain their upstream scale. Explicit snapshot sizes normally bypass
+the live-width override unless they match the world viewport's input dimensions.
+GPU texture, renderbuffer and viewport limits are checked. An unsupported request
+or allocation fallback disables the live override to avoid repeated allocation
+attempts. This does not guarantee protection against driver hangs or every memory
+failure in upstream's renderer. The control resets to Window on application restart.
+The Studio Actual World Buffer readout reports the allocated screen target size,
+rather than repeating the selected label. Existing resolution divisor/multiplier
+settings apply again when the live override is disabled.
+
+12K at 16:9 shades 84,934,656 pixels each frame, about 41 times 1080p. Deferred HDR,
+depth and postprocessing targets can consume several GiB beyond scene textures.
+This is an experimental source implementation, not a validated 12K gameplay build
+or a promise of good FPS on any GPU. No Windows compile or live GPU test was
+possible here. Validate allocation, scene/depth alignment, picking, UI composition,
+resizing, all postprocessing, reflection passes and FPS before using it routinely.
+
+Source validation: changed settings/XUI parse as XML; settings are declared and
+connected to the resize callback; selector widths and aspect calculations checked;
+patch whitespace and Windows helper shell syntax checked. Windows runtime tests
+and exact GPU output remain unverified.
